142	<section id="s1" class="part">
143	<h2>Landed since the curator&rsquo;s last approval</h2>
144	<p>Six items, not yet read, oldest first. The curator read items 41 and 42 at 22:23 UTC on 23 November 2026, so they went. At 00:1x UTC on 24 November the curator approved drafts 43 to 65, with the changes that he approved on their threads that evening, and they landed in one commit at 00:13 UTC. The words that he approved get no item. Each item below shows a passage whose landed words differ from them, against the approved words. In five passages, the approved words named the landing report or the gather record, both withdrawn on the drafts&rsquo; threads before the landing, at the curator&rsquo;s objection; the coordinator and the skill writer changed each by the fewest words. In one, a word changed for the skills&rsquo; lint.</p>
145	
146	<section id="l80" class="part item">
147	<h3><span class="num">Change 80 &middot; SKILL.md, glossary, &ldquo;default&rdquo;, line 32</span>A landed default is named in one line at the landing</h3>
148	<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">Landed text, against the approved words of draft 44; struck through, the approved words that went; underlined, the words that came in.</span>
149	<p class="where-in">SKILL.md, glossary, &ldquo;default&rdquo;, line 32</p>
150	<dl class="gloss"><dt>default</dt><dd>Option that stands unless the curator picks another: the one that an ask recommends, or the choice that an agent landed without the curator's word, which FACTS states and the landing <span class="cut">report</span> names <span class="cut">or counts.</span><span class="add">in one line.</span></dd></dl>
151	</div></div>
152	<div class="note"><p><strong>The withdrawn report.</strong> The approved words said that the landing report names or counts a landed default. That report was withdrawn before the landing, at the curator&rsquo;s objection: the post-batch review&rsquo;s section &ldquo;For the curator&rdquo; already tells him what each batch changed. So the entry now says that the landing names the default in one line, as step 2 of the landing now does for each decision that landed. The counts went with the report.</p></div>
153	</section>
154	
155	<section id="l81" class="part item">
156	<h3><span class="num">Change 81 &middot; SKILL.md, &ldquo;The curator&rsquo;s role and decisions&rdquo;, the three ways and the paragraph after them, lines 103 to 109</span>A landed decision is named in one line at the landing, in two places</h3>
157	<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">Landed text, against the approved words of draft 48; struck through, the approved words that went; underlined, the words that came in. In the skill&rsquo;s words, &ldquo;you&rdquo; is the coordinator.</span>
158	<p class="where-in">SKILL.md, &ldquo;The curator&rsquo;s role and decisions&rdquo;, the three ways and the paragraph after them, lines 103 to 109</p>
159	<p>It reaches the curator in one of three ways:</p>
160	<ol start="1"><li><strong>Asked before the work.</strong> A known fork is probed, and put as an ask before the batch is briefed.</li><li><strong>Landed, then asked.</strong> A decision that can be undone lands with its default, and <span class="cut">goes in the landing report.</span><span class="add">is named in one line at the landing.</span> Its question goes in the review queue, with the work that needs the answer, and stays there until the curator answers. Put the questions to the curator in the order of the work that needs them. A question that no work needs comes last.</li><li><strong>A hold.</strong> A decision that cannot be undone, or that acts against the curator's word, goes to the curator at once.</li></ol>
161	<p>Every other decision that changes the tree is closed when it lands. FACTS states it, and <span class="cut">it goes in the landing report.</span><span class="add">the landing names it in one line.</span> If it lands outside a batch, name it to the curator in one line, in your next message. A rung's small decisions go in the gap ledger, as rows. None of these holds up the work. If the curator objects to a decision that landed, open a review-queue item for it, and put it as your next ask. It is not a hold.</p>
162	</div></div>
163	<div class="note"><p><strong>The withdrawn report.</strong> The approved words sent a landed decision into the landing report twice: in the second of the three ways, and in the paragraph after them. That report was withdrawn before the landing, at the curator&rsquo;s objection. Both places now say that the landing names the decision in one line, the line that step 2 of the landing gives each decision. The rest of the passage landed as approved.</p></div>
164	</section>
165	
166	<section id="l82" class="part item">
167	<h3><span class="num">Change 82 &middot; SKILL.md, &ldquo;The curator&rsquo;s role and decisions&rdquo;, the bullet on changes that wait for the curator&rsquo;s yes, its first sentence, line 126</span>The landing&rsquo;s one line for each decision waits for the curator&rsquo;s yes</h3>
168	<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">Landed text, against the approved words of draft 49; struck through, the approved words that went; underlined, the words that came in. In the skill&rsquo;s words, &ldquo;you&rdquo; is the coordinator.</span>
169	<p class="where-in">SKILL.md, &ldquo;The curator&rsquo;s role and decisions&rdquo;, the bullet on changes that wait for the curator&rsquo;s yes, its first sentence, line 126</p>
170	<ul><li>A change that touches the curator's role and decisions (this section), the asks, the held list, the review queue, the <span class="cut">landing report</span><span class="add">landing's one line for each decision</span> or the register in which you write to the curator (the bullets at the head of "Talking to the curator") waits for the curator's yes to its exact words.</li></ul>
171	</div></div>
172	<div class="note"><p><strong>The withdrawn report.</strong> The approved words listed the landing report among the things whose change waits for the curator&rsquo;s yes. With the report withdrawn before the landing, the list names what took its place: the landing&rsquo;s one line for each decision, step 2 of the landing.</p></div>
173	</section>
