175	<section id="l83" class="part item">
176	<h3><span class="num">Change 83 &middot; references/batch.md, &ldquo;The go&rdquo;, the third bullet, line 39</span>One word for the skills&rsquo; lint: &ldquo;the batch&rdquo;</h3>
177	<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">Landed text, against the approved words of draft 60; struck through, the approved word that went; underlined, the word that came in.</span>
178	<p class="where-in">references/batch.md, &ldquo;The go&rdquo;, the third bullet, line 39</p>
179	<ul><li>If a question that the batch record raises is consequential (<code>SKILL.md</code>), put it to the curator first. Otherwise decide it. While the curator is away, overnight, take a consequential question's recommended default, and launch. Its question goes in the review queue, with <span class="cut">this</span><span class="add">the</span> batch as the work that needs it. If that default would reverse a decision of the curator, hold that batch, and launch the repair batch (<code>explorations/coordinator/REPAIR-BATCH.md</code>) in its place.</li></ul>
180	</div></div>
181	<div class="note"><p><strong>A word that goes stale.</strong> The skills&rsquo; lint flags &ldquo;this batch&rdquo; as wording that goes stale, since a skill outlives any one batch. The skill writer changed one word: the bullet now says &ldquo;the batch&rdquo;, the batch whose record raised the question. The rule does not change.</p></div>
182	</section>
