184	<section id="l84" class="part item">
185	<h3><span class="num">Change 84 &middot; references/batch.md, &ldquo;The roles&rdquo;, the third bullet, its sentences on a reserved point and a file outside the rung&rsquo;s section, line 55</span>A file outside a rung&rsquo;s section is listed in the post-batch review</h3>
186	<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">Landed text, against the approved words of draft 61; struck through, the approved words that went; underlined, the words that came in.</span>
187	<p class="where-in">references/batch.md, &ldquo;The roles&rdquo;, the third bullet, its sentences on a reserved point and a file outside the rung&rsquo;s section, line 55</p>
188	<p>Reaching a reserved point, or a file outside what the rung's section of the batch record names, does not make a settled fix contested: it lands. The point goes where "Reserved points and repairs" says, and the <span class="cut">gather record</span><span class="add">post-batch review's section "For the curator"</span> lists the file.</p>
189	</div></div>
190	<div class="note"><p><strong>The withdrawn term.</strong> The approved words had the gather record list a file that a rung changed outside its section of the batch record. The curator asked what the gather record was for, and its new glossary entry was withdrawn before the landing, since no rule needed the name. So the sentence now has the post-batch review list the file, in its section &ldquo;For the curator&rdquo;, where the curator reads what each batch changed.</p></div>
191	</section>
