194	<h3><span class="num">Change 85 &middot; references/batch.md, &ldquo;Reserved points and repairs&rdquo;, the first bullet, line 69</span>A reversible reserved point is named in one line at the landing</h3>
195	<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">Landed text, against the approved words of draft 63; struck through, the approved words that went; underlined, the words that came in. The third bullet of draft 63 landed as approved.</span>
196	<p class="where-in">references/batch.md, &ldquo;Reserved points and repairs&rdquo;, the first bullet, line 69</p>
197	<ul><li>A reversible reserved point does not hold the batch. The batch lands with the point's default, and the point <span class="cut">goes in the landing report.</span><span class="add">is named in one line at the landing.</span> If the point is consequential, such as a line of microGPT, its question also goes in the review queue. A point that is no decision, such as an output that a rung cannot explain, becomes a ledger row.</li></ul>
198	</div></div>
199	<div class="note"><p><strong>The withdrawn report.</strong> The approved words put a reversible reserved point in the landing report. That report was withdrawn before the landing, at the curator&rsquo;s objection. The point is now named in one line at the landing, as every decision that landed is. The rest of the bullet landed as approved: a consequential point also has its question in the review queue, and a point that is no decision becomes a ledger row.</p></div>
