375	<section id="words" class="part">
376	<h2>Words used on this page</h2>
377	<dl class="gloss">
378	<dt>coordinator</dt><dd>Coordinating session.</dd>
379	<dt>batch</dt><dd>Run of the batch workflow that takes several rungs at once, merges them and lands them together.</dd>
380	<dt>batch record</dt><dd>File that the planner writes before a batch&rsquo;s launch, whose rung sections are the workers&rsquo; briefs and whose other sections are for the curator.</dd>
381	<dt>PLAN</dt><dd>File of the record that holds the phases of the work, the questions for the curator in order, and the parked items.</dd>
382	<dt>PLAN&rsquo;s road</dt><dd>Work that the phases of PLAN list, in their order.</dd>
383	<dt>go</dt><dd>The curator&rsquo;s word that lets a batch or a new deliverable start.</dd>
384	<dt>rung</dt><dd>One piece of work in a batch, done by its own worker in its own worktree.</dd>
385	<dt>gather</dt><dd>Stage of a batch that merges the rungs, and folds their reports and record lines into the main tree.</dd>
386	<dt>manifest</dt><dd>Batch&rsquo;s list of its rungs, which the batch workflow reads.</dd>
387	<dt><code>landsOnlyWith</code></dt><dd>Field of the manifest that ties a rung to another, so that it lands only if the other lands too.</dd>
388	<dt>climb batch</dt><dd>Batch of PLAN&rsquo;s phases, numbered in order.</dd>
389	<dt><code>asif</code></dt><dd>Type assumption, written <code>e asif T</code>, which has a call treat the value of <code>e</code> as of its supertype <code>T</code>, to reach a supertrait&rsquo;s method; the code generator cannot compile it yet.</dd>
390	<dt>trait table</dt><dd>Code generator&rsquo;s table of an object&rsquo;s traits, which misses a trait in some objects that extend a trait of an imported api, and the name of the rung that fixes it.</dd>
391	<dt>main tree</dt><dd>Checkout of the repository at <code>/home/user/fortress</code>, not a worktree, where the gather and the stages after it work.</dd>
392	<dt>worktree</dt><dd>Second checkout of the repository in a folder of its own, where one agent works apart from the others.</dd>
393	<dt>skeptic</dt><dd>Agent that checks a rung&rsquo;s result after its worker, and fixes what it finds, test first.</dd>
394	<dt>point to report</dt><dd>Change of a kind that the curator reviews after the landing, which a rung lists with its evidence.</dd>
395	<dt>held push</dt><dd>Push of a batch that the batch workflow holds back, which leaves the batch&rsquo;s commits on the local <code>main</code> only.</dd>
396	<dt><code>pushHeld</code>, <code>heldBy</code></dt><dd>Fields of the batch workflow&rsquo;s result: whether it held the push, and the points that held it.</dd>
397	<dt>post-batch review</dt><dd>Check of a landed batch by one Opus reviewer, step 3 of the landing.</dd>
398	<dt>standing go</dt><dd>Go given once, in a skill, which holds for every case that it names.</dd>
399	<dt>hold</dt><dd>Decision that the work waits on until the curator answers.</dd>
400	<dt>judge, in a batch</dt><dd>Agent that rules on a fix that a skeptic contests, on a rung that the skeptic refuses, or on a rung whose worker could not go on.</dd>
401	<dt>skill writer</dt><dd>Headless session that makes every edit of the project skills.</dd>
402	<dt>compaction</dt><dd>Summary of the coordinator&rsquo;s conversation that replaces it when its context fills.</dd>
403	<dt>boot</dt><dd>Steps that the coordinator takes at session start and after each compaction, before any other work.</dd>
404	<dt>light boot</dt><dd>Earlier form of the boot, at the curator&rsquo;s word, that left FACTS, POSITIONS and INDEX unread and searched them instead; since 16 November 2026, the name of no form in the skill.</dd>
405	<dt>full boot</dt><dd>Boot that reads FACTS whole in place of the facts that POSITIONS cites, and INDEX whole; the default before 16 November 2026, and since then only at the curator&rsquo;s word.</dd>
406	<dt>FACTS</dt><dd>File of the record that holds what the project has established, <code>FACTS.md</code>.</dd>
407	<dt>POSITIONS</dt><dd>File of the record that holds the project&rsquo;s decisions, <code>POSITIONS.md</code>.</dd>
408	<dt>INDEX</dt><dd>File of the record that lists its entries by subject.</dd>
409	<dt>batch landing</dt><dd>End of a batch, when its commit stage ends and the chain of steps that brings the record in line starts.</dd>
410	<dt>context</dt><dd>Coordinator&rsquo;s working memory between two compactions.</dd>
411	<dt><code>facts-extract.sh</code></dt><dd>Script that searches the record and prints the matching entries.</dd>
412	<dt><code>positions-facts.sh</code></dt><dd>Script that prints the FACTS entries that POSITIONS cites, each whole, in numbered slices, for the first step of the boot.</dd>
413	<dt>slice</dt><dd>Numbered piece of a script&rsquo;s long output, printed one at a time.</dd>
414	<dt>permission check</dt><dd>Check of the session that allows or refuses each command before it runs.</dd>
415	<dt>cloud container</dt><dd>Virtual machine with its own disk, on which a cloud session of Claude Code runs, such as the coordinator&rsquo;s.</dd>
416	<dt><code>cloud-container</code></dt><dd>Skill that holds how the cloud platform behaves, for every agent that works in a cloud container.</dd>
417	<dt>scratch branch</dt><dd>Branch made only for a test, with no work on it to keep.</dd>
418	<dt>record</dt><dd>Project&rsquo;s memory: the files under <code>explorations/</code> that hold what the project has established, decided and measured.</dd>
419	<dt>tree</dt><dd>Repository&rsquo;s files and git history as they stand.</dd>
420	<dt>ask</dt><dd>Decision that the coordinator puts to the curator in chat, with its options and a recommendation.</dd>
421	<dt>close</dt><dd>Proposed end of an open item, such as one on the closing docket.</dd>
422	<dt>held list</dt><dd>List of the points that the curator raises while reading turn by turn, and of the rules that the curator states, kept until the coordinator acts on them or they enter a skill.</dd>
423	<dt>review list</dt><dd>List in the plan of the decisions already taken that waited for the curator&rsquo;s review; since 24 November 2026, the name of nothing in the skill.</dd>
424	<dt>review queue</dt><dd>File of the record that holds each question waiting for the curator&rsquo;s word, numbered and sorted by theme: <code>explorations/coordinator/review-queue.md</code>.</dd>
425	<dt>landing report</dt><dd>Message to the curator after each batch landing, on what a program does differently now, which the drafts of 23 November 2026 proposed and which was withdrawn before they landed.</dd>
426	<dt>landing&rsquo;s one line</dt><dd>Line that names one decision that landed, in step 2 of the landing.</dd>
427	<dt>&ldquo;For the curator&rdquo;</dt><dd>Section of the post-batch review that tells the curator in plain sentences what each rung changed in the language or the compiled code, and each fork that landed at its default.</dd>
428	<dt>gather record</dt><dd>File that the batch workflow writes once, at a batch&rsquo;s end, <code>RECORD.md</code> in the batch&rsquo;s folder; not the batch record.</dd>
